                     Excelsior! Picture Previewer v1.0
                        Copyright 1993 Sean Workman
                     AmigaX BBS 503-342-2144 16.8k DS
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
5/13/93

What is this?

This archive is presented to you for a couple of reasons.  The main reason
is to give you, another E! Sysop, an opportunity to see how my latest
program works.  As you might have guess, it's a picture previewer.  What
you might not have guessed was how it works.  No, it doesn't create ANSI
representations of the pictures, it merely scales down the existing picture
into a MUCH smaller (and quicker to transfer) preview that can be
downloaded (credit free to your users).  The benefits of this are mainly
for people calling either long distance and/or at lower baud rates (2400
baud and below).  By only downloading the preview of the picture, they
might know after 30 secons that they don't want to download a certain
picture that might have taken 5+ minutes otherwise...

Why did you distribute it as a bunch of pictures?

I program in Arexx.  I'm asking a shareware fee of $5 for EPP.  A very fair
fee considering the power of the program.  Ever try distributing a
shareware Arexx program?  Forget about it...  Arexx is about the easiest
language to 'uncripple' programs that there is...  so, with this particular
package, ONLY the registered users will have the source code (or should I
say program...)

Is it intelligent?

Yes.  EPP knows whether a picture is an IFF or a GIF file and converts it
automatically to IFF in the previewing process (this could be changed if
there was enough demand for GIF previews remaining in GIF format...)  It
also knows if the picture(s) have been archived or not.  Multiple pictures
of IFF and/or GIF formats are also handled correctly.  Future support for
JPeg is also planned but currently not implemented.

Will I get support if I register it?

You'll have access (free) to download the newest version of EPP until the
year 2064 when your registration contract will expire.  New terms will be
arranged at that time.  New versions will be available for download on my
BBS (AmigaX) or can be uuencoded through Usenet if need be.

Have you had much experience writing Excelsior! doors?

Well, I've written a handful of programs for Excelsior! so far.  I've
written Excelsior! Poker Solitaire, Excelsior! Last Caller, Maze-Craze,
Pathfinder, Logfile Filer (yet to be released), and LhaDo (yet to be
released BBS ad adder/remover).  I'm working on a shareware package for E!
sysops that would include registered versions of all the above mentioned
programs plus a detailed list of hints, tips, and tricks to running
Excelsior! to its full potential.

